<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Morgan cuts Hongkong Land.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Morgan cuts Hongkong Land.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>J.P. Morgan said it had downgraded Hongkong Land Holdings Ltd from buy to market performer, predicting that the stock would fluctuate around fair value of US$3.20-3.40.</p>
<p>The investment bank said it had made the downgrade in the light of the sharp rise in the stock this month and the prospect of falling book value with the office cycle likely to trend down in 1998.</p>
<p>Hongkong Land rose sharply last week on news Cheung Kong and Hutchison Whampoa had bought just over three percent. It closed on Friday at $3.30.</p>
<p>-- Ben Hirschler, London newsroom +44 171 542 6414</p>
